<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine 9-mth trade deficit at $9.132 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippine 9-mth trade deficit at $9.132 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' merchandise trade deficit widened to $9.132 billion for the first nine months of 1996 compared with $6.408 billion in the year-earlier period, the National Statistics Office said on Friday.</p>
<p>MERCHANDISE TRADE  Jan-Sept 96   Jan-Aug   Jan-Sept 95</p>
<p>    Exports		14.926	 13.051	12.802</p>
<p>    Imports		24.059	 21.206	19.210</p>
<p>    Trade balance	-9.132	 -8.155	-6.408</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billion U.S. dollars.</p>
<p>The NSO said the trade deficit reached $977 million in September alone compared with $849 million in the year-earlier month.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE    Sept 96  Aug 96   Sept 95</p>
<p>    Exports		   1,876    1,774    1,595</p>
<p>    Imports		   2,853    2,796    2,444</p>
<p>    Trade balance	    -977   -1,022     -849</p>
<p>Note - Figures in million U.S. dollars are rounded off.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937 Fax 817-6267</p>
